From: Zack Maril <zmaril@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:47:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] headstart: a paused compilation gives up its job slot

With `-Zearly-metadata`, rustc announces when it pauses, waiting for a
dependency's full metadata or rlib (`wait-metadata`), and when it
continues (`resume`). A paused unit no longer counts as running, so its
job slot goes to other work.

A resumed unit counts as running again at once, without waiting for a
free slot: waiting for one starved it, since work started in its place
held the slots, often while it was on the critical path. Cargo starts no
new work until the number of running units is back under the limit, so
the build can briefly run one unit over it.

